;; ESH-0101 guard coverage — FAIL-CLOSED probe.
;; An uncaught (error ...) must be fatal and must name itself on stderr.
;; Deliberately ONE argument: the VM's `error` is a fixed 1-argument native,
;; so a multi-irritant call could fail this probe at COMPILE time and be
;; graded "fails closed" for a reason that says nothing about whether an
;; unhandled condition is fatal at RUN time. (The gate rejects a compile-phase
;; failure outright for the same reason; irritant coverage lives in
;; 11_error_irritants.esk.)
(display "BEFORE ")
(error "fatal probe message")
(display "MUST-NOT-PRINT")
